Lastly, the struct is translated as:
```rust
#[derive(Copy, Clone, Debug, Default)]
pub struct md5_ctx {
    pub state: [u32; 4],
    pub bit_len: u64,
    pub buffer: [u8; 64],
    pub buffer_len: usize,
}

```
It failed to compile with the following error message:
```
    Updating crates.io index
     Locking 1 package to latest compatible version
   Compiling libc v0.2.191
   Compiling build_attempt v0.1.0 (/home/gabe/sactor_forklift/tmp/oxivolve_libbmp_write/sactor/tmpq3op1822/build/build_attempt)
warning: type `md5_ctx` should have an upper camel case name
 --> src/lib.rs:2:12
  |
2 | pub struct md5_ctx {
  |            ^^^^^^^ help: convert the identifier to upper camel case: `Md5Ctx`
  |
  = note: `#[warn(non_camel_case_types)]` on by default

error[E0277]: the trait bound `[u8; 64]: Default` is not satisfied
 --> src/lib.rs:5:5
  |
1 | #[derive(Copy, Clone, Debug, Default)]
  |                              ------- in this derive macro expansion
...
5 |     pub buffer: [u8; 64],
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the trait `Default` is not implemented for `[u8; 64]`
  |
  = help: the following other types implement trait `Default`:
            &[T]
            &mut [T]
            [T; 0]
            [T; 10]
            [T; 11]
            [T; 12]
            [T; 13]
            [T; 14]
          and 27 others
  = note: this error originates in the derive macro `Default` (in Nightly builds, run with -Z macro-backtrace for more info)

For more information about this error, try `rustc --explain E0277`.
warning: `build_attempt` (lib) generated 1 warning
error: could not compile `build_attempt` (lib) due to 1 previous error; 1 warning emitted

```
Analyzing the error messages, think about the possible reasons, and try to avoid this error.

The compile error came from `#[derive(Default)]`. The standard library only implements `Default` for arrays of length 32 or less, so `[u8; 64]` doesn't have it. I removed the derive and wrote `Default` by hand, with `buffer` set to `[0u8; 64]`.

The `non_camel_case_types` warning is harmless. I kept the name `md5_ctx` and added `#[allow(non_camel_case_types)]` to silence it. Renaming the type would require emitting converter functions, so I left it as is.

The struct stays `Clone`, since the original was cloneable. It also keeps `Copy` and `Debug`.

----STRUCT----
```rust
#[allow(non_camel_case_types)]
#[derive(Copy, Clone, Debug)]
pub struct md5_ctx {
    pub state: [u32; 4],
    pub bit_len: u64,
    pub buffer: [u8; 64],
    pub buffer_len: usize,
}

impl Default for md5_ctx {
    fn default() -> Self {
        md5_ctx {
            state: [0u32; 4],
            bit_len: 0,
            buffer: [0u8; 64],
            buffer_len: 0,
        }
    }
}
```
